# Line endings are a repo rule, not a per-machine setting: every text file is
# stored LF and checked out LF, whatever a contributor's core.autocrlf says.
# eol=lf (not merely text=auto) is what makes the working-tree guarantee hold.
# Binary content is exempted by git's own detection, with the format belt below
# for binary formats whose first bytes can read as text; validate_plugin's
# line-ending check fails any file whose INDEX bytes carry CRLF without a
# deliberate -text attribute here — so an accidental CRLF is a blocked commit,
# and a byte-preserving exemption is a visible decision in this file. That
# check also refuses a nested .gitattributes and any eol=crlf override: this
# file is the whole policy.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Format belt: known binary formats are exempt by NAME, not only by content
# sniffing — text=auto's NUL-in-the-first-8kB heuristic can misread a binary
# whose header is printable (and would then rewrite its CR/LF bytes). Formats,
# not paths: a path inventory of binaries rotted from 12 entries to 39 on the
# branch that first carried this policy; an extension names every future file
# of its kind wherever it lands.
*.png -text -eol
*.jpg -text -eol
*.jpeg -text -eol
*.gif -text -eol
*.webp -text -eol
*.ico -text -eol
*.woff -text -eol
*.woff2 -text -eol
*.ttf -text -eol
*.otf -text -eol
*.eot -text -eol
*.pdf -text -eol
*.zip -text -eol
*.gz -text -eol
*.tar -text -eol

# The roundtable gate hashes .karta files as the bytes on disk and compares them
# with what git will commit; a clean filter or EOL conversion would make git store
# different bytes than the gate approved. Keep every .karta path free of all
# three: -eol as well, so the `*` line's eol=lf cannot even APPEAR in this
# path's resolved attributes (it is inert while text is unset on git >= 2.10,
# but an inert ambiguity is still an ambiguity, and pre-2.10 gits read it).
# validate_plugin asserts this resolution on a live sentinel at every commit.
.karta/** -text -filter -eol

# Vendored font assets keep their upstream bytes exactly — the OFL license
# texts ship with CRLF and renormalizing a vendored file would make our copy
# diverge from the artifact it vendors. Same rule in each committed projection
# of the skill (the mirrors are byte-identical copies of the canonical tree).
skills/karta-status/assets/fonts/** -text -eol
.agents/skills/karta-status/assets/fonts/** -text -eol
plugins/karta/skills/karta-status/assets/fonts/** -text -eol
